### 9. Front matter capture: `MarkdownEventsReader`

File: `crates/liwe/src/markdown/reader.rs`

The parser is configured with YAML metadata support:

```rust
Parser::new_ext(
    content,
    Options::ENABLE_YAML_STYLE_METADATA_BLOCKS
        | Options::ENABLE_WIKILINKS
        | Options::ENABLE_TABLES,
)
```

When a metadata block starts:

```rust
Tag::MetadataBlock(_) => self.metadata_block = true,
```

When text is encountered while inside the metadata block:

```rust
Text(text) => {
    if !self.metadata_block {
        ...
    } else {
        self.metadata = Some(text.to_string());
    }
}
```

When the metadata block ends:

```rust
TagEnd::MetadataBlock(_) => self.metadata_block = false,
```

So the graph stores the raw YAML text inside the front matter block, not a parsed YAML object.

Relevant functions:

1. `MarkdownEventsReader::read`
2. `MarkdownEventsReader::start_tag`
3. `MarkdownEventsReader::end_tag`
4. `MarkdownEventsReader::metadata`

